      <isactr:ConnectorActivity.FieldObjects>
        <isactr:FieldObject Name="prompt" Type="FieldArgument">
          <isactr:FieldObject.Value>
            <InArgument x:TypeArguments="x:String" xml:space="preserve">["Extract the permit reference number from the supplied scanned document.

WHERE TO LOOK:
Look in the box in the TOP-RIGHT corner labelled ""PERMIT/CERTIFICATE"".

The required reference number is the text immediately following ""No.""

IMPORTANT:
- Do NOT extract the separate 6-digit number printed above the box.
- The reference number is normally 13 characters long.
- It follows this format:

\b2\dGB(IMP|EXP|A10|REX|POC|MIC)[A-Z0-9]{6}\b

- It starts with two digits followed by GB.
- The next three characters identify the permit type.
- The final six characters are letters or numbers.
- Pay particular attention to distinguishing O from 0.

VALIDATION:
Check that the extracted reference number matches the specified format before returning it.

OUTPUT:
Return ONLY the reference number.
If it cannot be confidently identified, return NOT_FOUND."]</InArgument>
          </isactr:FieldObject.Value>
        </isactr:FieldObject>
        <isactr:FieldObject Name="image_type" Type="FieldArgument">
